      "problem": "Calculate the value of $\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{3}{8}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We write $\\frac{1}{6}$ as $\\frac{4}{24}$ and $\\frac{3}{8}$ as $\\frac{9}{24},$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{24}-\\frac{9}{24}=\\frac{4-9}{24}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $4-9$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/3f5b60548cfd0332c74508678de51481f9fa149466c7d7880217b905e4d3891a.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-9}{24}=\\frac{-5}{24}=-\\frac{5}{24}.\n$$",
